#
# Pinned conda toolchain inputs -- the one place the base image and Miniforge
# release are recorded. This file is the reference for the pin; nothing else
# restates it.
#
# CONFIRMED GREEN: 2026-08-19. The docker build chain builds clean on the values
# at the bottom of this file. Until that date the pin was only *inferred* good
# from the registry push timeline, which is a weaker claim than this file is
# allowed to make -- see HOW TO MOVE THE PIN, step 3.
#
# WHY THIS FILE EXISTS
# --------------------
# On 2026-08-04 a working `scripts/build.sh docker` started failing inside
# `src/autonomous-trust/Dockerfile-devel`'s `conda env update`, with an upstream
# conda defect (`ZstdError: decompressed output exceeds 16777216 bytes` out of
# conda's sharded-repodata reader, whose 16 MiB cap is a hard-coded constant).
# Nothing in the repo had changed. The build was not reproducible: every conda
# input was floating.
#
#   - `FROM condaforge/miniforge3` was untagged, and `latest` had been re-pushed
#     that same day at 15:01 UTC -- roughly six hours before the failing build.
#   - `conda install -n base conda-rattler-solver` (since removed, see below)
#     carried no version bound and re-solved the base env as a side effect,
#     which is how base conda reached the 26.7.0 in the traceback; the base
#     image itself ships an older conda.
#   - `scripts/setup-dev.sh` fetched the Miniforge installer from
#     `releases/latest/download`, and both it and `src/Dockerfile-build` ran an
#     unbounded `conda update -n base conda`.
#
# A TAG ALONE IS NOT ENOUGH. Miniforge re-pushes image tags: `26.3.2-3` was
# released 2026-06-01 but its image was rebuilt 2026-08-04, picking up fresh
# conda-forge packages under an unchanged tag. Reproducibility therefore needs
# the digest, and `MINIFORGE_IMAGE` below carries both.
#
# WHAT IS PINNED, AND TO WHAT
# ---------------------------
# 26.1.1-3, whose image was pushed 2026-04-21 -- the base-image state in force
# during the window when the devel build was last green (2026-04-21 through
# 2026-08-04). Deliberately NOT the versions in the traceback quoted above:
# those are the failing ones.
#
# The digest is registry-specific. `MINIFORGE_DIGEST` is the Docker Hub
# manifest-list digest, because the Dockerfiles' bare `condaforge/miniforge3`
# resolves there; the same tag on quay.io has a different manifest-list digest
# (sha256:a2f0bbf1...), so do not mix the two.
#
# CONSUMERS -- all of these must agree, and `test_toolchain_pins.py` fails if
# they drift:
#   - src/autonomous-trust/Dockerfile-devel   ARG MINIFORGE_IMAGE default
#   - src/autonomous-trust/Dockerfile         ARG MINIFORGE_IMAGE default
#   - src/Dockerfile-build                    ARG MINIFORGE_IMAGE default
#   - scripts/build-docker.sh                 passes --build-arg MINIFORGE_IMAGE
#   - scripts/setup-dev.sh                    MINIFORGE_VERSION installer URL
#   - scripts/ci-local.sh                     conformance container default
#   - .github/workflows/{tests,conformance}.yml   miniforge-version:
# The Dockerfiles keep the value as an ARG *default* so a bare
# `docker build -f ... .` (as documented in their own headers) is pinned too,
# not only builds driven through build-docker.sh.
#
# HOW TO MOVE THE PIN
# -------------------
# 1. Pick the candidate release and read its Docker Hub manifest-list digest:
#
#      curl -s https://hub.docker.com/v2/repositories/condaforge/miniforge3/tags/<tag> \
#        | python3 -c 'import json,sys; d=json.load(sys.stdin); print(d["digest"], d["last_updated"])'
#
# 2. Edit the three values here AND the three Dockerfile ARG defaults AND the
#    three `miniforge-version:` lines, then run
#    `pytest src/autonomous-trust/tests/a_unit/test_toolchain_pins.py` -- it is
#    the only cheap check that they all still say the same thing.
# 3. Prove it with a real build before committing the new value:
#    `scripts/build-docker.sh --force devel test`, plus `builder` / `release` if
#    those are exercised. A pin recorded here that has not survived a green
#    build is the exact failure mode this file exists to prevent, so move the
#    CONFIRMED GREEN date at the top in the same edit -- or delete it, if the
#    new value has not built yet.

MINIFORGE_VERSION=26.1.1-3
MINIFORGE_DIGEST=sha256:958d2675e9a43e199cc85345ff4c60796236b651a9da4982765d99bd34a682d1
MINIFORGE_IMAGE=condaforge/miniforge3:26.1.1-3@sha256:958d2675e9a43e199cc85345ff4c60796236b651a9da4982765d99bd34a682d1
